          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">2. Gating Core Activation Features Behind Paywalls:</strong> Locking features that are required to achieve the "Aha!" moment inside paid tiers suppresses PQL rates. <em>Mitigation:</em> Keep core activation features free; gate volume, team collaboration permissions, and audit logs.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">3. Premature Sales Hand-off Before PQL Milestone:</strong> Routing unactivated signups to outbound SDRs creates massive sales overhead and high prospect annoyance. <em>Mitigation:</em> Enforce algorithmic PQL gating in HubSpot/Salesforce—AEs may only contact accounts with \( \Phi(X) > 0.65 \).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">4. Destructive Trial Expiration (Lockout vs Soft Downgrade):</strong> Locking users completely out upon trial expiration destroys organic reactivation. <em>Mitigation:</em> Transition expired workspaces to read-only or restricted free tiers to preserve user relationships and future upgrade triggers.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 my-6">
          <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">Can an enterprise sales motion coexist with a Reverse Trial?</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Yes. Leading modern PLG companies use the Reverse Trial as an organic lead generation engine for enterprise sales. When an individual account logs multiple users from the same corporate email domain (@company.com), automated routing flags the account as a Product Qualified Account (PQA) and alerts enterprise account executives for consolidated procurement outreach.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">How long should a Reverse Trial last?</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Empirical data suggests 14 days is optimal for standard B2B SaaS. 7-day trials truncate activation velocity for complex products, while 30-day trials dilute conversion urgency and extend the sales cycle unnecessarily.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">How do credit card requirements upfront impact downstream churn?</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Upfront credit card requirements dramatically reduce initial signups (by 60-80%), but yield higher trial-to-paid conversion (50-60%). However, Month 1-2 churn among credit card trials is up to 3x higher due to "accidental auto-renewals" and subsequent refund requests.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>

  <script is:inline>
    function updateSim() {
      const signups = parseFloat(document.getElementById('sim-signups').value) || 0;
      const archetype = document.getElementById('sim-archetype').value;
      const arpu = parseFloat(document.getElementById('sim-arpu').value) || 0;

      let convRate = 0.025;
      let freeCogs = 0.80;
      let cacEst = 250;

      if (archetype === 'freemium') {
        convRate = 0.025;
        freeCogs = 0.80;
        cacEst = 280;
      } else if (archetype === 'optin_trial') {
        convRate = 0.045;
        freeCogs = 0.10;
        cacEst = 320;
      } else if (archetype === 'reverse_trial') {
        convRate = 0.085;
        freeCogs = 0.50;
        cacEst = 350;
      }

      const paidAdds = Math.round(signups * convRate);
      const freeUsers = signups - paidAdds;
      const newMrr = paidAdds * arpu;
      const freeDrag = Math.round(freeUsers * freeCogs);
      const netMonthly = Math.max(1, (newMrr * 0.82) - freeDrag);
      const payback = (paidAdds * cacEst) / netMonthly;

      document.getElementById('out-paid-adds').innerText = paidAdds.toLocaleString() + ' accounts';
      document.getElementById('out-new-mrr').innerText = '$' + Math.round(newMrr).toLocaleString() + ' / mo';
      document.getElementById('out-free-drag').innerText = '$' + freeDrag.toLocaleString() + ' / mo';
      document.getElementById('out-payback').innerText = payback.toFixed(1) + ' Months';
    }

    document.getElementById('sim-signups')?.addEventListener('input', updateSim);
    document.getElementById('sim-archetype')?.addEventListener('change', updateSim);
    document.getElementById('sim-arpu')?.addEventListener('input', updateSim);
  </script>
</Layout>
